  "label": "child is mapped as the one asking the question",
  "description": "The text 'mommy, why am i getting christmas presents in august?' is directly addressed to the child in the image, who is visibly distressed and crying. The child is the subject of the question, and the visual material of the crying child is mapped onto the textual entity 'me' (implied by 'i') in the question. The child's emotional state (distress) is central to the mapping, as the question is posed from the child's perspective.",
